<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="18.11.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" Version="4.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="4.0.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="coverlet.collector" Version="10.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The sample project itself, not a copy of it. If the sample stops compiling or its flow
      changes shape, these tests fail — which is the only way a reference application stays a
      reference rather than becoming stale documentation. In particular the plan and the
      dispatcher these tests drive are the generated ones, so a [StreamTrigger] that stopped
      being read would fail here rather than at somebody's deployment.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../../samples/realtime-stream/RealtimeStream.csproj" />

    <!--
      The stream engine. FlowStreamScan is what these tests are about: FlowTestHost has no
      journal seam and no stream seam at all, so it cannot start this sample's flow.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/FlowX.Hosting/FlowX.Hosting.csproj" />

    <!--
      The test context the platform ships, used where it can be: the capability-level tests are
      profile-independent, so they need a CapabilityContext and nothing else. The windowing tests
      cannot use FlowTestHost — it has no journal seam and no stream seam, so it cannot start a
      Streaming flow at all.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/FlowX.Testing/FlowX.Testing.csproj" />

    <!--
      The conformance suite's reference journal and lease store, for tests/Workflow.Tests'
      reason: a second in-memory journal would be one nothing holds to the conformance suite,
      and the first thing it would drift on is StartAsync's refusal of a duplicate instance id
      — which is the behaviour every deduplication assertion here rests on.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../FlowX.Conformance.Tests/FlowX.Conformance.Tests.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
